  "description": "VELOCI WILDMOVE is built for riders who like going deeper into rough roads, forest trails, and long off-road routes without overcomplicating things. Whether set up for lightweight bikepacking, fully loaded touring, or simple trail riding, WILDMOVE is designed to stay capable, stable, and dependable across different terrain.\n\nThe frame and fork are constructed from double- and triple-butted 4130 CR-MO tubing with ED coating inside and out for long-term durability and corrosion resistance. The hardtail design keeps the bike simple, practical, and easy to maintain while still handling demanding riding conditions well.\n\nIts geometry uses a slightly longer wheelbase and lower bottom bracket height to improve stability on technical terrain and during loaded riding, helping the bike stay predictable on long descents, rough trails, and uneven surfaces.\n\nCurved fork legs and the negative angle dropout design help reduce vibration and trail chatter during long rides, giving the bike a smoother and more controlled ride feel without losing responsiveness. The lower-profile frame design also increases standover clearance, making technical riding feel more natural and easier to manage.\n\nMultiple cage and rack mounts on both the frame and fork allow flexible setup options for touring, camping gear, extra water, or everyday carrying needs. WILDMOVE blends ideas from touring bikes and mountain bikes into something versatile enough to adapt to different riding styles and environments.\n\nThe 44mm headtube and suspension-corrected geometry also make it easy to swap the rigid fork for a suspension fork if you want a more trail-focused setup later on.\n\nSimple, durable, and highly adaptable, WILDMOVE is made for riders who enjoy exploring further without worrying too much about what the road turns into next.",
